  "body": "No platinum label just yet, but this changes a lot and not all changes\nwere done manually so review is appreciated.\n\nThis should resolve these bugs:\n\nhttps://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=26400\nhttps://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=26402\n\nThere is definitely room for future cleanup:\n- Stop using the “resulting URL string” and “resulting URL record”\n  concepts in most scenarios. Assigning the result to a variable is\n  clearer.\n- Make encoding a more explicit argument (though keep the appropriate\n  defaulting).\n- Perhaps split “parse a URL” into an algorithm that takes an element\n  and another that takes a base URL.\n- Figure out if more places ought to invoke the URL parser directly (in\n  particular standalone APIs where we want to use UTF-8 as encoding\n  rather than defaulting.)\n",
